docs/guide.md:41:After developing the Proofbound CLI itself, the local/global refresh flow is:
docs/guide.md:44:npm --prefix packages/main run build
docs/guide.md:45:npm install -g ./packages/main
docs/guide.md:46:lattice --version
docs/guide.md:47:lattice check
docs/guide.md:48:lattice doctor --format=json
docs/guide.md:49:lattice rollout_check --projects "$(pwd)" --json
docs/guide.md:52:`rollout_check` is a read-only cross-project inspection: it reads Git state, managed asset state, runtime footprint, and story/transcript scope readiness, and outputs each project's `status` and `nextAction`. It never runs `check --apply`, `check --upgrade`, repair/fix, third-party installers, evidence submission, or receipt verification. The main repo can be PASS; external projects, old wrappers, or non-git projects are interpreted as WARN/FAIL with a next step, rather than forcing the user to run doctor/check one by one and guess at the cause.
docs/guide.md:54:### Local Proof Admissibility
docs/guide.md:56:Server-backed authority modes and receipt commands are retired from the active Proofbound CLI. Active evidence vocabulary is `admissibilityStatus`, `assuranceLevel`, `evidenceScope`, gate-consumed local evidence, signed/offline receipt bundles, and local review quorum assurance.
docs/guide.md:58:### Autopilot Mode: Local Only
docs/guide.md:60:`lattice autopilot` is the local unattended-development control surface.
docs/guide.md:63:lattice autopilot status --json
docs/guide.md:64:lattice autopilot doctor --json
docs/guide.md:65:lattice autopilot run --mode=local --storyId=B-xxxx --until=TEST --json
docs/guide.md:66:lattice autopilot execute --mode=local --storyId=B-xxxx --until=TEST --maxSteps=20 --json
