docs/guide.md:87:lattice planner run --request="<one sentence>" --mode=local --until=DONE --json
docs/guide.md:92:- `planner draft` / `review` / `status` / `source-manifest` are read-only; `planner create-story` / `create-job` write state only through Proofbound commands.
docs/guide.md:93:- Interaction mode is `--interactionMode=autonomous|interview|decision-gated` (default `autonomous`); a paused run resumes with `planner answer` / `planner decision submit` / `planner resume`.
docs/guide.md:94:- `planner run` strings together draft → review → Story → local plan → executor, but DONE is still bound by the same local gates as autopilot. Treat it as the planning entry point, not a guarantee of unattended DONE.
docs/guide.md:96:### Multi-host verdicts and run status
docs/guide.md:98:Release certification can require independent local host verdicts:
